 seal:{t:'475-3\u2033 seal gas',d:['To EX/C-1121 seals \u00B7 injection tubing','HANDWRITTEN FIELD NOTE (PetroSkills Ch.22 source): residue gas is used for seal gas on this unit \u2014 consistent with the manual\u2019s point that plant outlet gas is a common real-world seal gas source since it\u2019s already clean, dry and near ambient temperature.']},
 lube:{t:'Lube oil console',d:['2\u00D715 HP pumps \u00B7 lube tank PSV (PSV-1121A)']},
 v1421:{t:'V-1421 \u2014 Cold Separator (020185-AE-DW-M2135, Rev 10)',d:['108\u2033 ID \u00D7 20\u2032-0\u2033 S/S \u00B7 1100 psi DP @ \u221250/150\u00B0F \u00B7 2.5\u2033CU insulation, no heat trace \u2014 RE-VERIFIED this session, nameplate matches exactly, no changes needed',
  'Vapor \u2192 EX-1121 expander normally; at low flow, bypasses via JT valve straight to T-1521 feed instead',
  'Liquid \u2192 directly to T-1521 (via line 444-10\u2033, entering the tower at a mid/upper feed point) in C2 recovery mode, OR to E-1223/1224 side reboiler (via line 434-12\u2033) in C2 rejection mode. CORRECTED this session \u2014 previously said the recovery path went through E-1222 (reflux condenser); the real P&ID\u2019s own continuation callout for line 444-10\u2033 points directly at T-1521, not E-1222.',
  'Level instrumentation: LSHH-1421 uses a thermal probe type in an external cage (confirmed real, already correctly documented); 2\u00d7LT-1421 for normal level control.']},
 lcvA:{t:'LCV-1421A C2 recovery valve',d:['\u2192 433-8\u2033 \u2192 444-10\u2033 \u00B7 HS-1421 (REC) \u2192 directly to T-1521 (drawing M2150), NOT via E-1222 \u2014 confirmed this session from the real P&ID\u2019s own continuation callout, correcting the related `proc_cryomode` entry which previously said E-1222']},
 lcvB:{t:'LCV-1421B recovery',d:['\u2192 432-6\u2033 to E-1221/22 \u00B7 Note 5 close on low FT-1222']},
 warm:{t:'TCV-1421 cold-spin valve',d:['TIC-1421 controlled cold-spin/warm-gas valve on the top dry-gas path to V-1421 \u00B7 observed SP -30 F / PV about -7.2 F / CV 0% \u00B7 opens when PV falls below SP']},
 pt1421:{t:'PT-1421 separator pressure',d:['PAH/PAL \u00B7 PY-1121A/SY-1121 \u2192 expander']},
 v1421lt:{t:'V-1421 level instruments',d:['2\u00D7LT-1421 \u00B7 LSHH-1421 thermal probe, external cage']},

 v1443:{t:'V-1443 \u2014 Refrigerant Reclaimer',d:['13.75\u2033 OD \u00D7 7\u2032-6\u2033 S/S \u00B7 PV/270 psig @ -60/150\u00B0F','46 KW electric heaters (HE-1443A/B) boil off liquid propane carried over with compressor oil, leaving oil behind','Flashed propane vapor recovered to V-1441 suction \u00b7 recovered lean oil sent directly back to the compressors',
  'Confirmed real (Ryan, direct dictation, 7/23/2026): a small ~1\u00bd\u2033 line ties the chiller/refrigeration circuit into V-1443 -- receives propane contaminated with compressor lube oil, heats/vaporizes the propane for recovery, and retains the heavier oil for controlled draining. General refrigeration-reclaimer operating principle only -- exact Clear Fork piping detail, heating-source confirmation, and drain procedure/interval are Pending Verification, not guessed.',
 ]},
 suct601:{t:'601/621-24\u2033 refrig suction',d:['V-1443 \u2192 C-1141/C-1140 (M2210/M2225) \u2014 OPEN']},
 refl:{t:'Refrigerant level valve',d:['Propane level into E-1241 shell \u2014 OPEN upstream']},
 hvr:{t:'Hot vapor recycle (turndown)',d:['PCV-1441 hot-gas bypass \u2014 NORMALLY NO FLOW']},
 psvV:{t:'V-1443 / chiller-side PSV',d:['SET POINT: 230 psig \u00B7 PCV-1443 failure case']},
 exp_cascade:{t:'EX-1121 Expander \u2014 CASCADE Mode (CTRL-001, engineering inference)',d:[
  'CASCADE is a mode of AUTO on the ACMTC IGV controller: PIC-1521 (demeth tower pressure) becomes the cascade primary, writing its own remote setpoint into the expander IGV target -- matching this simulator\u2019s own reference text describing "a cascade flow controller taking its remote setpoint from a plant pressure controller."',
  'Direction/gain used (opening the IGV further when tower pressure runs high, giving the expander more relief-path capacity) is an ENGINEERING INFERENCE based on standard split-range pressure-relief convention -- it has NOT been independently verified against a real control narrative document. Classification: Requires Verification if a real cascade control philosophy document becomes available.',
  'CASCADE only engages when AUTO is also selected (same as a real DCS, where cascade is a sub-mode of auto, not a separate mode); switching to MAN always drops CASCADE back to off. Plain AUTO and MAN behavior are completely unchanged when CASCADE is off -- this was verified by testing IGV response before/after the feature was added.'
 ]},
 mval:{t:'Manual block valve (typ.)',d:['Gate / ball isolation per P&ID','Shown collectively on the Manual valves layer', 'Line isolation, bypass blocks, drains and vents']},
