var CF_PID_M2150_12IB=cfUnpackStatic12KG({"number":"020185-AE-DW-M2150","revision":"2","page":"1-2 (two scans of the same drawing)","title":"T-1521 Demethanizer / Cryogenic Unit #1","sourceFile":"2026-10-05 22-43.pdf","sha256":"46e4ea22d0d808ac4338607d72e39f8836e4bb3496a0507c344a67e4845fcefa","issueMarking":"ISSUED FOR CONSTRUCTION","reviewed":"2026-10-05","sourceRetained":false,"sourceStorageMode":"learn-only","scope":"Source-specific readback of both scans. Main tower and existing connected routes retained; added local outlet/check/bypass/drain/sample and temperature graphics are schematic. No new control/interlock or approved field procedure. Fine unreadable notes remain pending.","facts":[{"id":"identity","tags":["T-1521"],"text":"Both pages show M2150 Revision 2, Issued for Construction, T-1521 DEMETHANIZER. They are two scans of one sheet, not two towers. FV-5030A is a separate stabilizer-return photo and is not a demethanizer valve.","location":"Title block, equipment heading and separate photo","status":"DRAWING_READBACK / FIELD_VERIFICATION_PENDING"},{"id":"vessel_envelope","tags":["T-1521"],"text":"The heading shows a 108/72-inch two-diameter vessel and 550 PSI DP. Small S/S length, temperature and insulation digits require a clearer source before superseding older transcriptions. The illustrated shell narrows below the upper section; the existing simulator display envelope is retained, not certified as a dimensionally exact pressure vessel. Drawn fill/dump ports and internal indications are not newly modeled as verified mechanical internals.","location":"Vessel outline, heading and side connection annotations","status":"DRAWING_READBACK / FIELD_VERIFICATION_PENDING"},{"id":"overhead","tags":["450","E-1222","T-1521","PT-1521D"],"text":"450-18-inch-CS-B0-304SS-4.5-inchCU is the overhead connection to E-1222 on M2130. The 18-inch downcomer/nozzle annotation and pressure instrument connection are distinct from the incoming lower feeds. This source does NOT route demethanizer overhead to the C-5700 stabilizer overhead compressor; that older generic INFO statement is retained only as superseded history.","location":"Top-left overhead line and pressure tap","status":"DRAWING_READBACK / FIELD_VERIFICATION_PENDING"},{"id":"cold_feeds","tags":["562","420","427","444","T-1521"],"text":"Four separate lower feed connections are retained in order: 562-8-inch from E-1222, 420-8-inch from E-1222, 427-14-inch from EX/C-1121, and 444-10-inch from V-1421. Their 8/8/14/10-inch downcomer markings remain source facts, not justification for changing all upstream piping. Existing RSV, GSP, expander/JT and cold-separator identities stay distinct.","location":"Four upper/middle left-hand continuations","status":"DRAWING_READBACK / FIELD_VERIFICATION_PENDING"},{"id":"side_reboiler","tags":["436","437","E-1224"],"text":"436-12-inch-CS-B0-304SS-3.5-inchCU goes toward E-1224 and is marked FREE DRAINING. The local 14x16 annotation is adjacent to its minimum-height/downcomer detail. 437-14-inch-CS-B0-304SS-2.5-inchCU returns from E-1224 and is marked DO NOT POCKET. These are separate draw/return connections, not one collapsed pipe.","location":"Middle-left side-reboiler connections","status":"DRAWING_READBACK / FIELD_VERIFICATION_PENDING"},{"id":"bottom_reboiler","tags":["439","441","E-1223","E-1225"],"text":"439-12-inch-HL-B0-LT-1.5-inchCU goes toward E-1223, is marked FREE DRAINING and references Note 2 with a local 12x16 annotation. 441-14-inch-HL-B0-LT-1.5-inchCU returns from E-1225 and is marked DO NOT POCKET. Note 2 full installation wording remains pending; existing routing is not certified as satisfying a minimum vertical run.","location":"Lower-left bottom-reboiler draw and trim return","status":"DRAWING_READBACK / FIELD_VERIFICATION_PENDING"},{"id":"equalization","tags":["534","T-1521","V-1422"],"text":"534-10-inch-HL-B0-LT-1-inchCU is the separate EQUALIZING LINE between T-1521 and V-1422 on M2155, marked DO NOT POCKET. The PSV pressure takeoff is on this equalizing circuit, not the separate overhead line 450. The existing model has a top-root PSV and a high equalizing nozzle: this source-placement discrepancy is explicitly flagged, not represented as a verified match.","location":{"$kg":1317},"status":"DRAWING_READBACK / FIELD_VERIFICATION_PENDING"},{"id":"psv","tags":["PSV-1521","2310","2309","2311","2312"],"text":"PSV-1521 is annotated 6-inch Class 300 inlet x 8-inch Class 150 outlet, SET @ 550 PSIG, PCV-1121A FAILURE. Pressure comes from line 534 through 6-inch CSO inlet isolation 2310. Half-inch bleed 2311 is on the inlet side. Outlet-side half-inch bleed 2312 precedes 8-inch CSO outlet block 2309; an 8-to-12-inch enlargement joins 1076-12-inch-DC-A0-304SS to DC / M2260. This is drawing reference data, not a new trip, current valve lineup or relief-capacity assessment.","location":"Upper-right PSV cloud","status":"DRAWING_READBACK / FIELD_VERIFICATION_PENDING"},{"id":"psv_vent","tags":["2308","1076","534"],"text":"A separate 4-inch CSC manual vent 2308 branches from line 534 and rejoins the relief outlet AFTER PSV outlet block 2309. It is not a second PSV and not a demonstrated RF main-flare tie. The original model flare-collector connection is retained but flagged as unresolved versus this DC/M2260 source. New relief-side valves remain source-only until this mismatch is resolved.","location":{"$kg":1318},"status":"DRAWING_READBACK / FIELD_VERIFICATION_PENDING"},{"id":"bottom_pressure","tags":["2301","PT-1521A"],"text":"Half-inch CSO pressure-root valve 2301 is shown on the lower equalizing-line pressure tap feeding PT-1521A and its PI/PAH/PAHH indications. Alarm labels are not numerical trip settings; no values are inferred.","location":"Lower-right pressure instrument branch","status":"DRAWING_READBACK / FIELD_VERIFICATION_PENDING"},{"id":"bottom_temperature","tags":["TE-1521F","TW-1521F","TE-1521E","TW-1521E"],"text":"TE/TW-1521F and TE/TW-1521E are separate temperature assemblies on the lower outlet system, with distinct TI and high/low alarm indications. Their two representative thermowell/head graphics preserve separate IDs; no new calibration, range or live alarm limit is created.","location":"Lower-right paired temperature instruments","status":"DRAWING_READBACK / FIELD_VERIFICATION_PENDING"},{"id":"bottoms_outlet","tags":["504","518","XV-1521","2305"],"text":"The bottom nozzle is marked 12 inch and leads to 504-10-inch-HL-B0-LT-1.5-inchCU. The paired temperature taps are upstream of 10-inch check 2305, followed by existing XV-1521 marked 10-inch FC. Downstream service is 518-10-inch-HC-B0-CS-1.5-inchCU to V-1422 on M2155. The LT/CS service break is retained as reference data; it is not a new control loop.","location":"Lower-right main liquid outlet","status":"DRAWING_READBACK / FIELD_VERIFICATION_PENDING"},{"id":"outlet_bypass","tags":["2306","XV-1521","2307"],"text":"One-inch CSC manual bypass 2306 bypasses XV-1521 only and rejoins downstream. It does not bypass upstream check 2305. The separate 0.75-inch low-point drain 2307 branches between check 2305 and XV-1521. Drain terminal destination is not established by this sheet. The model includes only a local labelled termination, not an invented flare or closed-drain header connection.","location":"XV-1521 local bypass and low-point branch","status":"DRAWING_READBACK / FIELD_VERIFICATION_PENDING"},{"id":"sample","tags":["2304","AE-1521"],"text":"A distinct one-inch sample-point valve 2304 and AE-1521 / GC connection lie downstream of XV-1521, with Note 3. The local sample branch is modeled without inventing an analyzer enclosure or sample-return destination; Note 3 full dimensions/wording remain pending.","location":"Far-right outlet sampling station","status":"DRAWING_READBACK / FIELD_VERIFICATION_PENDING"},{"id":"dryout","tags":["590","2303","F-1416","F-1417"],"text":"590-1-inch-GP-D0-CS from F-1416/F-1417 on M2105 is the DRYOUT / LIFT GAS SUPPLY. Valve 2303 and Note 4/Note 6 appear at its tie into the bottom outlet before the temperature/check/shutdown assembly. It is not a vent or a new third JT/expander feed route. Its complete field route and fine note wording remain source-only.","location":"Bottom dryout line and vertical tie","status":"DRAWING_READBACK / FIELD_VERIFICATION_PENDING"},{"id":"overhead_roots","tags":["2300","215001","215002","PT-1521D"],"text":"The overhead circuit includes a separate half-inch capped branch 2300 and half-inch pressure-root / bleed entries 215001 and 215002 at the PT/PI-1521D assembly. The capped branch is not a proven drain destination and the signal line is not process piping.","location":"Upper-left to top-center instrumentation","status":"DRAWING_READBACK / FIELD_VERIFICATION_PENDING"},{"id":"interfaces","tags":["XXY-1521","ZSO-1521","ZSC-1521"],"text":"XV-1521 has XXY-1521 solenoid/signal representation, ZSO-1521 and ZSC-1521 position indications and instrument-air connection. The drawing does not replace the existing simulator trip/sequence implementation or establish a new operating permission. EPC/Exterran boundaries are retained as source boundaries, not another isolation valve.","location":"XV-1521 actuation and package boundaries","status":"DRAWING_READBACK / FIELD_VERIFICATION_PENDING"}],"lines":[{"number":"450","nominalInches":18,"specification":"CS-B0-304SS-4.5CU","upstream":"T-1521 overhead","downstream":"E-1222 / M2130"},{"number":"562","nominalInches":8,"specification":"CS-B0-304SS-2.5CU","upstream":"E-1222 / M2130","downstream":"T-1521 upper feed"},{"number":"420","nominalInches":8,"specification":"CS-B0-304SS-2.5CU","upstream":"E-1222 / M2130","downstream":"T-1521 GSP feed"},{"number":"427","nominalInches":14,"specification":"CS-B0-304SS-4CU","upstream":"EX/C-1121 / M2145","downstream":"T-1521 expander/JT feed"},{"number":"444","nominalInches":10,"specification":"CS-B0-304SS-2.5CU","upstream":"V-1421 / M2135","downstream":"T-1521 liquid feed"},{"number":"436","nominalInches":12,"specification":"CS-B0-304SS-3.5CU","upstream":"T-1521 side draw","downstream":"E-1224 / M2140 printed continuation; cross-sheet identifier to verify"},{"number":"437","nominalInches":14,"specification":"CS-B0-304SS-2.5CU","upstream":"E-1224 / M2165","downstream":"T-1521 side return"},{"number":"439","nominalInches":12,"specification":"HL-B0-LT-1.5CU","upstream":"T-1521 bottom draw","downstream":"E-1223 / M2165"},{"number":"441","nominalInches":14,"specification":"HL-B0-LT-1.5CU","upstream":"E-1225 / M2140","downstream":"T-1521 trim return"},{"number":"534","nominalInches":10,"specification":"HL-B0-LT-1CU","upstream":"T-1521 lower equalizing connection","downstream":"V-1422 / M2155; equalizing service"},{"number":"1076","nominalInches":12,"specification":"DC-A0-304SS","upstream":"PSV-1521 / manual vent outlet","downstream":"DC / M2260"},{"number":"504","nominalInches":10,"specification":"HL-B0-LT-1.5CU","upstream":"T-1521 bottoms","downstream":"XV-1521 upstream / 518 transition"},{"number":"518","nominalInches":10,"specification":"HC-B0-CS-1.5CU","upstream":"XV-1521 downstream","downstream":"V-1422 / M2155"},{"number":"590","nominalInches":1,"specification":"GP-D0-CS","upstream":"F-1416 / F-1417 / M2105","downstream":"T-1521 bottoms outlet dryout/lift tie"}],"valves":[{"tag":"2300","nps":0.5,"kind":"manual","service":"Overhead separate capped small branch","location":"Upper-left overhead","marking":"Capped; current position not asserted","equipment":"T-1521"},{"tag":"215001","nps":0.5,"kind":"manual","service":"PT-1521D overhead pressure root","location":"Overhead pressure assembly","marking":"","equipment":"T-1521"},{"tag":"215002","nps":0.5,"kind":"manual","service":"PT-1521D overhead small bleed","location":"Overhead pressure assembly","marking":"","equipment":"T-1521"},{"tag":"2310","nps":6,"kind":"manual","service":"PSV-1521 pressure-side inlet isolation","location":"PSV pressure branch on 534","marking":"CSO","equipment":"T-1521"},{"tag":"2311","nps":0.5,"kind":"manual","service":"PSV-1521 inlet-side bleed","location":"After inlet block, before PSV","marking":"","equipment":"T-1521"},{"tag":"2312","nps":0.5,"kind":"manual","service":"PSV-1521 outlet-side bleed","location":"After PSV, before outlet block","marking":"","equipment":"T-1521"},{"tag":"2309","nps":8,"kind":"manual","service":"PSV-1521 outlet isolation","location":"After PSV before DC enlargement","marking":"CSO","equipment":"T-1521"},{"tag":"2308","nps":4,"kind":"manual","service":"Separate equalizing-line manual vent to DC","location":"534 to downstream side of outlet isolation","marking":"CSC","equipment":"T-1521"},{"tag":"2301","nps":0.5,"kind":"manual","service":"Lower equalizing pressure root to PT-1521A","location":"Lower right pressure tap","marking":"CSO","equipment":"T-1521"},{"tag":"2303","nps":1,"kind":"manual","service":"Dryout / lift-gas tie isolation","location":"590 supply into bottoms outlet","marking":"","equipment":"T-1521"},{"tag":"2305","nps":10,"kind":"check","service":"Demeth bottoms check upstream of XV-1521","location":"Main outlet after temperature taps","marking":"","equipment":"T-1521"},{"tag":"2307","nps":0.75,"kind":"manual","service":"Low-point drain between check and XV-1521","location":"Bottoms liquid outlet","marking":"LOW POINT DRAIN","equipment":"T-1521"},{"tag":"2306","nps":1,"kind":"manual","service":"Manual bypass around XV-1521 only","location":"Bypass rejoins downstream, after check","marking":"CSC","equipment":"T-1521"},{"tag":"2304","nps":1,"kind":"manual","service":"NGL outlet sample isolation","location":"Downstream of XV-1521","marking":"SAMPLE POINT","equipment":"T-1521"},{"tag":"XV-1521","nps":10,"kind":"shutdown","service":"Demethanizer NGL outlet shutdown valve","location":"After check and before sample","marking":"FC","equipment":"T-1521"},{"tag":"PSV-1521","nps":6,"kind":"psv","service":"Demethanizer equalizing pressure-zone relief","location":"Equalizing line 534 / DC to M2260","marking":"550 PSIG; PCV-1121A FAILURE","equipment":"T-1521"}],"instruments":[{"tag":"PT-1521D","kind":"instrument","service":"Overhead pressure transmitter","location":"Top-center pressure assembly","equipment":"T-1521"},{"tag":"PI-1521D","kind":"instrument","service":"Overhead pressure indication","location":"Top-center signal","equipment":"T-1521"},{"tag":"PDI-1521","kind":"instrument","service":"Tower differential-pressure indication","location":"Vertical differential-pressure signal","equipment":"T-1521"},{"tag":"PT-1521A","kind":"instrument","service":"Lower equalizing pressure transmitter","location":"Lower pressure root","equipment":"T-1521"},{"tag":"PI-1521A","kind":"instrument","service":"Lower pressure indication/alarm interfaces","location":"Lower pressure signal","equipment":"T-1521"},{"tag":"TE-1521F","kind":"instrument","service":"First lower-outlet temperature element","location":"Main liquid outlet upstream of check","equipment":"T-1521"},{"tag":"TW-1521F","kind":"instrument","service":"First lower-outlet thermowell","location":"Same physical assembly as TE-1521F","equipment":"T-1521"},{"tag":"TI-1521F","kind":"instrument","service":"First outlet temperature indication","location":"Temperature signal","equipment":"T-1521"},{"tag":"TE-1521E","kind":"instrument","service":"Second lower-outlet temperature element","location":"Main liquid outlet upstream of check","equipment":"T-1521"},{"tag":"TW-1521E","kind":"instrument","service":"Second lower-outlet thermowell","location":"Same physical assembly as TE-1521E","equipment":"T-1521"},{"tag":"TI-1521E","kind":"instrument","service":"Second outlet temperature indication","location":"Temperature signal","equipment":"T-1521"},{"tag":"XXY-1521","kind":"instrument","service":"Shutdown-valve solenoid/interface","location":"XV-1521 actuator signal","equipment":"T-1521"},{"tag":"ZSO-1521","kind":"instrument","service":"XV-1521 open-position indication","location":"XV-1521 actuator","equipment":"T-1521"},{"tag":"ZSC-1521","kind":"instrument","service":"XV-1521 closed-position indication","location":"XV-1521 actuator","equipment":"T-1521"},{"tag":"AE-1521","kind":"instrument","service":"GC sample-point analyzer interface","location":"Downstream 518 sample branch","equipment":"T-1521"}],"pending":["PSV-1521: M2150 shows takeoff on lower equalizing circuit 534 and discharge DC/M2260. The legacy 3D symbol is top-rooted and its continuation goes to a schematic flare collector. This mismatch is explicitly NOT fixed by merely adding source metadata; field/continuation-based rerouting is still required.","The legacy uniform T-1521 model envelope is not a mechanical reproduction of the source 108/72-inch two-diameter vessel. No global rescale, nozzle move or internals fabrication is claimed.","Source line 436 border references M2140 while retained E-1224 source context uses M2165; printed continuation is retained and cross-sheet reconciliation remains pending.","Vessel S/S length, heading temperature/insulation digits, small detail labels and the full wording of Notes 2-6 remain pending clearer source readback. Free-draining / DO NOT POCKET labels do not certify existing routing.","Drain/sample terminal destinations, valve manufacturer subtypes, schedules, actual ODs, insulation, supports and field elevations are not established. Local open-ended graphics are labelled pending, not connected to a guessed service.","No numerical alarm/trip setting, live valve position, actuator failure action beyond an explicit source FC marking, or approved isolation sequence is inferred.","Existing whole-network contact candidates are separate from this local update and remain review items. No Navisworks coordinates were decoded."]});
